doc.snippet:

MCP Tool Pattern:
- Tools live in src/mcp/tools/, registered via functions like registerUserTools(server, userService).
- Input and output schemas are defined with Zod for validation and documentation.
- Tools delegate to service layer (e.g., UserService) and return both text content and structuredContent.

Example:
export function registerUserTools(server: McpServer, userService: UserService) {
  server.registerTool(
    'list_users',
    {
      title: 'List Users',
      description: 'List all users with optional search filter',
      inputSchema: { ... },
      outputSchema: { users: z.array(UserSchema) }
    },
    async ({ search, max }) => {
      const users = await userService.list({ search, max });
      return {
        content: [{ type: 'text', text: JSON.stringify(users, null, 2) }],
        structuredContent: { users }
      };
    }
  );
}
